      "content": "idk, some people argue that if it's just about \"cultural capital\" or \"familiarity,\" then the gap shouldn't be so persistent or deep. wouldn't there be more fundamental or biological differences that explain why the gap stays even when you control for things like school funding? some people say that testing is just a way to measure innate cognitive ability and the results reflect that reality.",
